(Routines are real calls, so recursion works. Variables are global,)
(so recurse "tail style": do the multiplying before the recursive call.)
(Variables shared by the whole program)
Let a number be called acc
Let a number be called n

routine fact:
    if n is greater than 1.0:
        multiply acc by n
        subtract 1.0 from n
        run fact

action start:
    set n to 10.0
    set acc to 1.0
    run fact
    print "10! = ", acc
